\ Phase 7 slice 5: `tabulate` — allocate an array and fill each slot by
\ splicing an inline quotation that produces a fresh value.  Each slot gets
\ a distinct, freshly-constructed value (never a replicated one), so a linear
\ element type is safe once the destructor lands (Phase 4 of this slice).
\
\ This example uses `i64` (a `Copy` element) so it builds and runs today; the
\ linear-element golden is Phase 4's exit (the destructor does not exist yet).

import: intrinsics * ;
import: core::prelude * ;

\ Build a 5-element array where each slot holds its own index.
: main ( -- )
  5 ~[ 42 ] tabulate | arr |
  &arr 0 >usize &> @ .
  &arr 1 >usize &> @ .
  &arr 2 >usize &> @ .
  &arr 3 >usize &> @ .
  &arr 4 >usize &> @ .
  arr drop ;
